At ten in the morning, the train entered the ghat mountains.
The train went slowly up into the mountains.
The scenery outside had completely changed.
I looked outside from my own window.
This was the middle of the summer season.
Therefore, all the valleys were very dry.
I saw brown mountains there.
Everywhere there were large rocks and dry trees.
There were no clouds in the sky, only harsh sunlight.
In front of me, there was a boy.
His sister was also nearby.
That boy looked outside from her window.
That girl became angry.
She said, "This is my window."
"You look from your own window."
That boy sat sadly in his own seat.
I smiled gently.
I again looked outside from my own window.
These dry mountains were very beautiful in the sunlight.
